From cab756334d34ac0830f5de3ec1b44a2d5afc96e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 04:57:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stats/eventhandler: Track circuit failures with relay
 fingerprints

Add infrastructure so scanning modules can know which exit relays had
circuit failures and why:

stats.py:
- Add CIRCUIT_FAILURE_MAP translating Tor failure reasons to structured
  keys and human-readable messages
- Add circuit registry (register_circuit/resolve_circuit/complete_circuit)
  that maps circuit IDs to their intended first-hop and exit relay
- Add record_immediate_failure() for circuits that fail before getting an
  ID from the controller
- Add get_failed_circuit_relays() to retrieve failure details
- update_circs() now records failure details per exit relay

eventhandler.py:
- Pass first_hop fingerprint through module_call to probing modules
- Track pid_to_fingerprint mapping for process -> relay association
- Grace period in shutdown(): wait for straggling processes before
  terminating, collecting fingerprints of forcibly killed relays
- Enhanced teardown() callback: pass stats, controller, and
  terminated_relays to modules that accept keyword arguments
  (falls back to no-args call for backward compatibility)

exitmap.py:
- Use stats.register_circuit() when creating circuits so failures
  can be traced back to specific relays
- Use stats.record_immediate_failure() for instant creation failures
- Rejection sampling for random first-hop selection (avoids O(n)
  list copy + remove on every circuit)

Co-authored-by: 1aeo <1aeo@users.noreply.github.com>
